      <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-d693e8297b09403db5fc77c17ea396b5" textAlignment="1">
        <bounds x="396" y="12" width="325" height="97"/>
        <content>The L0 value stream is decomposed into L1 stages before linking them to L1 capabilities. By only linking same-level elements, COVO allows for consistent zooming across levels.</content>
      </child>
      <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-9a61cc23487f4ddc93390a7833da4dbe" textAlignment="1">
        <bounds x="396" y="132" width="325" height="241"/>
        <content>A capability can have one of three roles in each stage:&#xD;
&#xD;
1. Principal capability (e.g., C.1, C.3): Bears primary responsibility for the stage's outcome. When its object reaches the desired state, the stage exits.&#xD;
&#xD;
2. Enabling capability with co-manifestation (e.g., C.2): Manifests concurrently to enable the principal capability.&#xD;
&#xD;
3. Enabling capability without co-manifestation (e.g., C.4): Impacts value creation in this stage by having transformed its object outside the scope of this specific stage.</content>
      </child>
      <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-67ee7e92084040eaa8e6d2c0ad8fac60" textAlignment="1">
        <bounds x="396" y="420" width="325" height="205"/>
        <content>The object relationships are exact mirrors of the relationships between stages and capabilities. Their labels express the nature of their dependencies.</content>
      </child>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel" name="L1 Value Stream W" id="id-bcb44231ee9a465491fe3d66ded06166">
