      </child>
      <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-5893e8da6cee4f74900e91fd743fcdcf" textAlignment="1">
        <bounds x="192" y="12" width="325" height="373"/>
        <content>The capabilities at this level should provide a classification of activities based on Starreveld's value cycle. We will provide further guidance in the future. For now, we distinguish three primary domains:&#xD;
&#xD;
1. Supply or input: Activities needed to procure goods and services directly related to the organization's primary value propositions.&#xD;
&#xD;
2. Production or transformation: Core value-adding activities. These are modeled independently of the other two domains, which serve to integrate this core domain into its larger economic environment. Complex organizations providing value at multiple levels (e.g., ideas, physical products, services) may split this domain into multiple layers.&#xD;
&#xD;
3. Delivery or output: Customer interaction, including establishing agreements, invoicing, and providing customer care.&#xD;
&#xD;
Note that this example is limited to L1, but in practice, these capabilities are further refined to Level 2 or 3 to reach operational granularity.</content>
      </child>
    </element>
